I wasn't raging on you specifically or anything.  It's just a pattern that
I've noticed in general that puts a bad taste in my mouth.  So no worries.

Oops, my bad.  lo'ai cfalu sa'ai cfila le'ai

Also, I'm on the fence as to whether {lo te cfila} should be appended to the
end of my definition.

lo sisku cu sisku lo cfila ne'i lo te sisku ku ja'e lo te cfila

I'm pretty sure that's a terrible use of {ne'i} but I'm not sure which tag
would work best for "in/amongst" in this case.

